    "summary_one_sentence": "This archival documentary weaves together long-lost Las Vegas residency footage, rare film clips, and personal recordings to showcase Elvis Presley telling his own story in his own words.",
    "summary_short": "Unearthing long-lost performance footage from Elvis Presley's legendary 1970s Las Vegas residency, this documentary offers a fresh, intimate look at the King of Rock 'n' Roll. Interwoven with rare 16mm clips from 'Elvis on Tour' and 8mm home movies from the Graceland archives, the film highlights rare archival recordings discovered during research for Baz Luhrmann's 2022 biopic. Together, these elements allow Elvis to narrate his own journey during a pivotal era of his career. It delivers an unforgettable cinematic celebration of Presley's dynamic stage presence and personal history.",
    "summary_long": "EPiC: Elvis Presley in Concert brings audiences an unprecedented look at one of the most iconic performers in music history by utilizing previously thought-lost footage from his famous 1970s Las Vegas residency. Rather than relying solely on external commentators, the documentary relies heavily on rediscovered audio recordings of Elvis himself detailing his own side of the story, uncovered during the deep research phase for Baz Luhrmann's 2022 feature film, Elvis. Visually, the concert footage is complemented by rare 16mm material shot during his 'Elvis on Tour' period, capturing the raw energy of his traveling shows. Personal 8mm film clips sourced directly from the Graceland archives add a deeply personal contrast to his massive public persona. Viewers are taken on a journey through the highs and lows of his legendary live performances, witnessing his powerful vocals and magnetic stage movement up close. The film explores his connection with his fans, his dedicated backing band, and the intense pressure of constant performance during his later years. By combining these diverse visual formats, the production recreates the electrifying atmosphere of a live Elvis concert like never before. Ultimately, it paints a rich, multidimensional portrait of a cultural titan reclaiming his own narrative through his voice and music.",
    "synopsis": "EPiC: Elvis Presley in Concert is a captivating archival music documentary that brings the legendary King of Rock 'n' Roll back to the stage through rare, long-lost footage and intimate audio recordings. Sourced in part from research conducted for Baz Luhrmann's 2022 biographical film 'Elvis,' the project incorporates unseen recordings of Presley sharing personal reflections on his life and career. The visual backbone of the documentary consists of restored footage from his celebrated 1970s Las Vegas residency, interspersed with 16mm clips from 'Elvis on Tour' and candid 8mm home footage preserved in the Graceland archives. Designed as an immersive tribute, the film offers a spoiler-free, authentic look into the artistry, charisma, and personal world of Elvis Presley during one of the most defining performance eras of his life.",
